  "trend_reading": "Reported crashes fell from 37,918 in 2019 to a 26,155-28,003 band in 2020-2025, while fatal crashes were 100 in 2019, peaked at 126 in 2022-2023, and injury crashes stayed in a 7,462-9,189 band (2020-2025). Per-crash severity therefore reads higher after 2019. STRONGEST ALTERNATIVE EXPLANATION, carried not resolved: the mix of what gets reported may have changed (COVID-era volume drop in Mar-Jun 2020 is visible in the monthly series; minor-crash reporting thresholds and staffing are not in this dataset), so the claim is the two measured series (volume down, fatal/injury counts flat-to-up), never a claim that Nashville driving became more dangerous per mile - there is no exposure denominator in this layer",
